| `venv.extras` | list of strings | `["dev"]` in a generated project; keel's own lists `template` too, because its gate renders projects with copier | non-empty list of `pyproject.toml` optional extras, each a word with no spaces | `scripts/check_venv.py` | Sets the extras, beside the core dependencies, whose requirements `make check-venv` judges at the start of `make verify`, and the extras its pip command names; `dev` reaches `transport` through its own `<project>[transport]` entry. A keel venv without copier fails the check, rather than skipping every copier test. An extra `pyproject.toml` does not declare is refused with exit 14. Absent, the check writes `[using default] venv.extras = ["dev"]` to stderr. | a transport's packages: `transports.extras` | always |
